# /sdd-migrate

Purpose:
  Auto-generated purpose for sdd-migrate.

Owns: commands\sdd-migrate.sdd
Description:
  Run pending migrations after .sdd/ schema updates. Must be run after
  any .sdd/ update that changes file locations or schemas.

Usage:
  /sdd-migrate
  /sdd-migrate --list
  /sdd-migrate --apply=<id>
  /sdd-migrate --rollback=<id>

Options:
  --list      List pending and applied migrations
  --apply     Apply specific migration by ID
  --rollback  Rollback specific migration by ID

Migrations:
  Location: .sdd/projects/{project_name}/migrations/
  Format: sequential ID, description, applied_at

Exit Codes:
  0 - Success
  1 - Failed
  2 - No pending migrations
  3 - Already applied

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  Timeline: @../timeline/migrations.sdd
  Runtime: @../runtime/INDEX.sdd

State: +
